task: optics-verdict-refresh
agent: opus-optics
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/optics-verdict
worktree: ../okay-wt-verdict

why: four lanes today changed what an optic costs, and the verdict in
  specs/optics.md and docs/theory/10-optics.md is the one measured
  BEFORE any of them — "one field 1.7x, composed 3.5x, the bar was
  1.5x, so optics are a convenience layer and not a hot-path
  primitive". A reader gets advice that is no longer true, which is
  worse than no advice.

what: one full run of the optics suite on this tree, then the tables
  and the verdict rewritten from it. The OLD numbers stay, labelled
  as what the interpretation cost, because that is the record of why
  the fusion was built.

not: no code changes. If a number comes back worse than the old one,
  it goes in as it is.
